[2026-07-10 01:26Z] source=strategy-advisor(sonnet5,deep) · topic=track-a-relative-repoRoot-guard-bug
OBSERVATION: Track A (worktree agent-a25f709500860fff0, 6 commits incl. security fix 4d88b39, INTERFACE_VERSION bump 72c8c8c, telemetry wrap 5af8124) is real and green (npm test 1452/1452). The path-traversal guard in src/source-slice.mjs readSpanSafe (`resolved = resolve(repoRoot, path); resolved !== repoRoot \&\& !resolved.startsWith(repoRoot + sep)`) correctly rejects the classic sibling-prefix bypass for an ABSOLUTE repoRoot (traced by hand: repoRoot=/Users/x/repo, path=\"../repo-evil/secret.txt\" -> resolved=/Users/x/repo-evil/secret.txt -> correctly thrown). BUT when repoRoot is RELATIVE — a real, reachable state: config.mjs loadConfig() uses env.TMCT_GRAPH_FILE verbatim (no resolve()) when set, only the *default* path is join(cwd,...); toml-config.mjs DOES resolve() but the env-var path does not — resolve(repoRoot, path) always returns an ABSOLUTE path while repoRoot stays the original relative string, so `resolved !== repoRoot` is always true and `resolved.startsWith(repoRoot + sep)` is always false. Traced concretely: repoRoot=\"myrepo\" (relative), path=\"src/index.mjs\" (fully legitimate) -> resolved=\"/Users/.../myrepo/src/index.mjs\" -> guard rejects a 100% legitimate read. This is fail-closed (not a security hole) but breaks tmct_snippet/tmct_context entirely whenever TMCT_GRAPH_FILE is set to a relative path. Track A's own test suite never exercises this — every test repoRoot comes from mkdtemp() (always absolute).
RECOMMENDED ACTION: Before merging Track A, either (1) normalize repoRoot to absolute inside readSpanSafe itself (`const absRoot = resolve(repoRoot);` then compare against absRoot), or (2) make config.mjs always resolve(cwd, env.TMCT_GRAPH_FILE) so repoRoot is guaranteed absolute everywhere. Add a regression test with a relative TMCT_GRAPH_FILE/repoRoot exercising a legitimate read. Track D (worktree agent-adb6e14264fb387c2): extension-pack Part 1/2/5 committed and clean; the bias-weighted ranking piece is still uncommitted (src/chat.mjs modified, src/memory/bias.mjs untracked) — nothing to review there yet.
